-- Step 34: the company's cash and bank accounts, transfers between them, and expenses paid out of them.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/cash-bank/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by Drizzle.
-- Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A cash or bank account is an account of the chart under Cash accounts or Bank accounts; petty
-- cash is one more cash account. A bank account may have its bank and number written beside it.
-- A cash or bank account is archived only when everything ever posted to it adds up to nil.
--
-- A transfer (TR-) moves money between two of them:   debit the one it went to, credit the other.
-- An expense (EX-) spends money out of one of them:
--   debit   each expense line                       its amount, and its share of the province's tax
--   credit  Provincial sales tax withheld payable   the province's tax on services, withheld whole
--   credit  Income tax withheld payable             income tax, at the supplier's rate (s.153)
--   credit  the cash or bank account                what is left: what was paid
-- each from its dated line of Step 25's withholding tables, and only by a company that withholds.
-- Both are written, with their journal, by one function of the database's own; one entered by
-- mistake is cancelled with a reversal, never changed.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE300 to SE399 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE330  bank details belong to a bank account of the company
--   SE331  not one of the company's cash or bank accounts in use, or the same one twice
--   SE332  an amount, a reason or a transaction that will not do
--   SE333  a date that has not come yet, or before the document's own
--   SE334  no such transfer or expense in this company
--   SE335  already cancelled
--   SE336  a branch that is not one of the member's
--   SE337  paid to no one, or to two
--   SE338  tax withheld from no supplier, or by a company that does not withhold
--   SE339  an expense line, or a withholding, that will not do
--   SE340  a cash or bank account archived while it holds something
--   SE341  an archived account a cancellation would post to: restore it first
--   SE342  sent again with the same key but other figures: the first was recorded

-- ── generated by drizzle-kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

